 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Try to get inside view if you can. Ask friends and neighbors where they go, and if they have a good experience, ask why. Lots of them mean nothing until you see a place in person. Look for busy spots, a busy bar, and a restaurant that's not too quiet. It means they want you to try something new, not necessarily that there's bitage inflation. Go with something classic like pasta or chicken, and see if it feels expensive. You' be surprised how many turn out to be hidden gems. In the meantime, trust your gut and get a good room to watch from.",
